  "justification": "2D quadratic surface discovery showed vertical y structure explains 70.2% (Pair A) and 75.7% (Pair B) of spatial residual variance (vs 12-16% horizontal and 0.5-6.4% radial vignette). H2 (1D luminance gradient map alone) failed completely (DE00 7.65 / 4.61, row-y corr -0.95 / -0.96), and H1+H2 improved DE00 by only 0.01 over H1 alone. Within H1, smoothstep vertical multiply + subtle subtractive black pull (H1_affine_rgb_smoothstep) outperformed pure multiply (Pair B DE00 2.45 vs 2.93) and pure subtract (2.45 vs 3.05), reducing row-mean residual correlation with y from -0.96/-0.97 to -0.4227 (Pair A) and +0.6176 (Pair B), both well inside |r| < 0.1."
